      "instruction": "Which outfit will the tail wear?",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "prompt": "ev + lAr",
          "say": "evler",
          "options": [
            "evlar",
            "evler"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "explanation": "ev has one vowel — e. It’s a front vowel, so the e outfit: evler (houses)."
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "prompt": "okul + DA",
          "say": "okulda",
          "options": [
            "okulda",
            "okulde"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The last vowel is u. It’s a back vowel, so the a outfit: okulda (at school)."
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "prompt": "kız + lAr",
          "say": "kızlar",
          "options": [
            "kızlar",
            "kızler"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "ı has no dot. It is not the English i: it is a back vowel, like the a in about. So kızlar (girls)."
        },
        {
          "id": "4",
          "prompt": "vapur + (y)A",
          "say": "vapura",
          "options": [
            "vapura",
            "vapure"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The last vowel is u, a back vowel. The a outfit: vapura (to the ferry)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a1.harmony-2.ex2",
      "lesson": 1,
      "kind": "practice",
      "skill": "grammar",
      "type": "sort_buckets",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "instruction": "Which outfit will -lAr wear? Sort the words",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "buckets": [
            {
              "id": "a",
              "label": "a outfit: -lar"
            },
            {
              "id": "e",
              "label": "e outfit: -ler"
            }
          ],
          "entries": [
            {
              "text": "kitap",
              "bucket": "a"
            },
            {
              "text": "göl",
              "bucket": "e"
            },
            {
              "text": "kız",
              "bucket": "a"
            },
            {
              "text": "köy",
              "bucket": "e"
            },
            {
              "text": "saray",
              "bucket": "a"
            },
            {
              "text": "otel",
              "bucket": "e"
            },
            {
              "text": "kahve",
              "bucket": "e"
            },
            {
              "text": "telefon",
              "bucket": "a"
            }
          ],
          "explanation": "Look only at the last vowel. a ı o u are back vowels: the a outfit. e i ö ü are front vowels: the e outfit. kız has ı without a dot — back, so kızlar. göl and köy have dots — front. In otel and kahve the last vowel is e."
        }
      ]
    },
